  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1245 AM CDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nAn upper level ridge will continue to be centered northeast of \nour area through at least the middle of next week, and began \nexpanding further west later in the week. Highs once more will \ncontinue to range from the middle 90s to just above 100 degrees \neach day through the middle of next week. Heat indices will \ncontinue hovering around the 105-108 degree mark near the I-35 \ncorridor and coastal plains. Seabreeze showers and thunderstorms \ncould impact the coastal plains every afternoon into the evening. \nMost other locations should see mainly dry conditions. Towards the\nend of the forecast period models are hinting at a pattern shift \nwhich would finally drop temperature below 100 degrees and perhaps\nsee better chances for rain coverage over the area. Models \ncontinue to disagree on how this occurs so continue to check back \nas we get closer and models hopefully come into better agreement.",
